# Corpus unit stay-on-topic-with-classifier-free-guidance/C05 — gap (mandatory rater-power CQ unmet)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/stay-on-topic-with-classifier-free-guidance.yaml C05 (causal,
# blind_paired_human_evaluation; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: CFG with negative prompting
# improves assistant system-prompt following — at gamma=3 blind paired human evaluators prefer
# CFG completions 75% of the time over vanilla, while user-prompt relevance preference stays near
# 52% (approximately random), from 1,740 blindly judged prompt pairs (E05, Figure 5).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * The sample's single blind_paired_human_evaluation claim -> human_evaluation(S, B, Q, Exp),
#     conclusion preferred(S, B, Q). Bundled/conjunctive claim: the binding conjunct is the
#     positive system-prompt-following preference (the sample headline); the near-50% user-prompt
#     relevance null conjunct stays in nl and refs.
#   * human_evaluation's mandatory rater_power CQ (sufficient_raters) maps onto the annotation's
#     mandatory "per-gamma vote counts and evaluator counts sufficient, with variability for the
#     75/52 figures?" — annotated unmet-gap (E05 metrics list only total/unique vote counts; no
#     per-gamma sample size, CI, or test). The human_evaluation argument is therefore incomplete:
#     it is declared as a located hole with `open rater_power` (lowering re-done for issue #15
#     under lara-core@0.3); the claim stays `gap` on empty complete support.
#   * blinding (mandatory) is annotated met and its leaf is supplied. Post-hoc gamma=3 selection
#     maps to the OPTIONAL preregistration CQ (no status effect); the 52%-establishes-
#     non-degradation CQ is the null conjunct's equivalence question, outside the binding atom.
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact stay-on-topic-with-classifier-free-guidance at sha256:7d6532a2b09e
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, the positive preference conjunct --------------------------------------

claim c05
  nl      = "At gamma=3 blind paired human evaluators prefer CFG-with-negative-prompting completions for system-prompt following 75 percent of the time over vanilla, while user-prompt relevance preference stays near 52 percent; per-gamma vote counts and rater variability for the 75 and 52 figures are not reported and gamma=3 is the post hoc peak"
  formal  = preferred(cfg_negative_prompting, vanilla, system_prompt_following)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: E05's gamma=3 preference cell (75% system-prompt following), per result cell.
leaf e1 : reports(e05, human_preference(cfg_negative_prompting, vanilla, system_prompt_following, favorable))
  kind       = observed
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C05, logic/experiments.md#E05, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N12, Figure-5]

leaf e2 : blinded(e05)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E05-Procedure-step-3, logic/experiments.md#E05-Setup]

# --- ... but the argument is incomplete (a located hole) ----------------------------------------

# rater_power is open (no per-gamma vote counts, confidence intervals, or significance for the
# 75%/52% rates) and mandatory, so a1 is a hole; the optional preregistration (post-hoc gamma=3
# selection) is open too.
arg a1 : supports(c05) by human_evaluation(cfg_negative_prompting, vanilla, system_prompt_following, e05)
  discharge blinding        with e2
  open      rater_power
  open      preregistration

status c05

# ==============================================================================================
# EXPECTED VERDICT (golden oracle)
# ==============================================================================================
# Compiled AF: no arguments (the hole is not a node).
# Located hole: a1, open obligations [rater_power]; it sources no attacks.
# Claim status:
#   c05 -> gap (empty complete support; statusC = Gap iff null claimSupport, spec §8;
#          the located hole is reported in `holes`, not counted as support)
